WEBVTT

00:59:58.167 --> 01:00:01.059
And you put these people to work together?

01:00:01.083 --> 01:00:03.726
This is true in the classroom
and this is true at work.

01:00:03.750 --> 01:00:07.250
They are going to have
messages and meta messages.

01:00:08.625 --> 01:00:10.518
That's just a nutshell on a --

01:00:10.542 --> 01:00:12.393
AG: Alright.
(Laughter)

01:00:12.417 --> 01:00:13.768
So autonomy versus loyalty.

01:00:13.792 --> 01:00:15.309
What I think about is

01:00:15.333 --> 01:00:18.643
you don't have to give people
autonomy about the ends

01:00:18.667 --> 01:00:21.101
if you give them autonomy about the means.

01:00:21.125 --> 01:00:23.601
This is something one of my mentors,
Richard Hackman

01:00:23.625 --> 01:00:25.018
found throughout his career,

01:00:25.042 --> 01:00:27.309
that if leaders were
very clear about a mission,

01:00:27.333 --> 01:00:29.184
a purpose, a goal to work toward,

01:00:29.208 --> 01:00:31.684
they could give people
a ton of autonomy then